-- title:
--   Charts at every place not fixed by φ²
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$, a level $N \neq 0$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ which is surjective, together with modular polynomial data $\mathrm{data}$ of level $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence $\mathrm{hKr}$ (the bivariate reduction mod $q$ of $\Phi$ equals $(Y^{q}-X)(Y-X^{q})$), integrality hypotheses $h\alpha$, $h\beta$ for the Hecke homomorphisms $\overline{\alpha}$, $\overline{\beta}$ at level $N$ and $q$ over $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$, a place specialization $P$ for these data, and a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$. Assume given a fibre model $\mathrm{fm}$ of level $N$ over $A$ with reduction $\mathrm{red}$, equipped with a cusp chart $\mathrm{hcc}$ (so $\overline{j_N}\,\overline{j}^{-N}$ lies in the ring $B_\infty$ of $\mathrm{fm}$ and $\pi_\infty$ sends it to $j_{q,N}\,j_q^{-N}$ in characteristic $q$); modular polynomial data $\mathrm{dataAll}\,d$ for every nonzero $d \mid N$, with the level-$N$ polynomial, reduced mod $q$ and viewed over $\mathrm{RatFunc}\,k$, separable; the hypothesis $\mathrm{hP}$ that the specialization map $P.\mathrm{sp}$ is the map $\mathrm{fm}.\mathrm{spPlace}$ attached to $\mathrm{fm}$ by these data; $q \nmid N$; and the hypothesis $\mathrm{hBFC}$ that every element of the Laurent base change of the full level-$N$ modular function field which is a root of a monic polynomial over the subring $\mathrm{affineBaseFin}\,N\,A$ generated by the constants from $A$ together with $\overline{j}$ already lies in $\mathrm{fm}.B_{\mathrm{Fin}}$. Then $R$ has charts: for every place $v$ of the characteristic-$q$ level-$N$ function field over $k$ which is not fixed by the square of the geometric-level Frobenius map on places, there is a subset $S$ of the level-$Nq$ field over $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ which is a chart at $v$ for $R$.
--
--   This supplies the local charts used to recognise the prolongation tuple as a model of the special fibre of $X_0(Nq)$ at $q$ — two copies of $X_0(N)$ meeting at the supersingular points — at arbitrary level prime to $q$, rather than only at squarefree level; the cusp chart of the fibre model replaces the squarefree hypothesis, since at levels with a square factor some places above the cusps are not fixed by $\varphi^2$. It is used in the construction of a prolongation tuple which is a model and whose order law is fixed, [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.exists_prolongationTuple_isModel_and_orderLawFixed`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.exists_prolongationTuple_isModel_and_orderLawFixed).
